      (alarm log,
 42   recording search, keyframe stamps inside recordings) are that NVR's local clock and are
      converted with
 43   that NVR's UTC offset, which lensd learns from the NVR, before being stored or compared.
      Assumption: the
 44   offset is fixed (the site has no daylight saving) and is learned once (see Accepted
      behaviour).
 45
 46│  **Def $Time.Elapsed (elapsed time).** Timeouts, graces and watchdogs are measured on lensd's
   │  own monotonic
 47│  clock (`time.Since` of a `time.Now()` value), never by subtracting wall times that came from
   │  an NVR.
 48
 49   ### 0.2 Intervals and nearness
 50
 51   **Def $Interval (interval).** An interval [Start, End] is closed, with Start <= End. Zero
      length
 52   (Start = End) is valid: one instant.
 53
 54   **Def $Interval.Gap (gap, within).** For intervals A and B with A.Start <= B.Start, gap(A, B)
      = B.Start - A.End,
 55   negative when they overlap. "Within d" means gap <= d; "more than d apart" means gap > d.
      Every bound in
 56   this spec states whether it is inclusive; the default is inclusive at the top ("at most N",
      "<= 5 s").
 57   A fetch window [from, to) is half-open, so an event on a boundary belongs to exactly one
 lensd.spec.md     No baseline 46:1 | $Time.Elapsed                                |  1     0    0
